; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Morse Code Beeper
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     morse code, property list, words, timing
; SUMMARY:  Sends any message in Morse code as beeps and draws the dots and dashes on the screen as they are sent.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Morse code turns letters into short and long beeps: a dot (dit)
;   and a dash (dah). It was used on telegraph wires and ship radios
;   long before phones. The program looks up every letter of the
;   message in a property list, beeps it, and draws it: a round dot
;   for dit, a bar for dah, one row of the screen per word.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run with the sound on. To send your own message, type in the
;   command center:  send [your message here]
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a property list as a code book: letter in, code word out
;   * the code itself is a word like .-- that FOREACH can walk through
;   * Morse timing: a dah is 3 dits, gaps are 1, 3 and 7 dits long
;   * a list of words, and a word of letters, nested FOREACH loops
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make :dit 60 to send faster, like an expert operator.
;   * Add the digits: 1 is .----, 2 is ..---, up to 0 which is -----.
;   * Write a program that goes the other way: from dots to letters.
; ============================================================

make "dit 90        ; the length of one dot in milliseconds
make "pitch 650     ; radio operators liked a pitch around 600 to 800

to codebook
  localmake "table [a .- b -... c -.-. d -.. e . f ..-. g --. h ....
                    i .. j .--- k -.- l .-.. m -- n -. o --- p .--.
                    q --.- r .-. s ... t - u ..- v ...- w .-- x -..-
                    y -.-- z --..]
  ; the table alternates letter, code, letter, code ...
  while [not emptyp :table] [
    pprop "morse first :table first butfirst :table
    make "table butfirst butfirst :table
  ]
end

; One symbol: beep and draw. A dot is a round spot, a dash a bar.
to symbol :s
  ifelse :s = ". [
    setpensize 12 dot pos
    sound (list :pitch :dit 0 :dit)
    penup fd 20
  ] [
    setpensize 12 pendown fd 30 penup
    sound (list :pitch 3 * :dit 0 :dit)
    fd 20
  ]
end

to letter :ch
  localmake "code gprop "morse lowercase :ch
  if emptyp :code [stop]          ; skip anything not in the code book
  foreach :code [symbol ?]
  sound list 0 2 * :dit           ; 1 + 2 = 3 dits between letters
  penup fd 22
end

to send :message
  localmake "y 200
  foreach :message [
    setpencolor 2
    penup setxy -380 :y setheading 90
    label uppercase ?
    setxy -230 :y + 6
    setpencolor 6
    foreach ? [letter ?]
    sound list 0 4 * :dit         ; words are 7 dits apart
    make "y :y - 70
  ]
end

clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground [15 25 15]
setlabelheight 20
codebook
send [sos hello world from logo]
